From: KV260 image builder <builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] xrt: retain xclIPName2Index export for VART 3.5

VART 3.5 uses this two-argument edge API for compute-unit discovery.
XRT 2.18 retains its implementation but hides its C symbol. Restore only
this export for the pinned VART compatibility integration.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [VART 3.5 compatibility]
---
 runtime_src/core/include/deprecated/xrt.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/runtime_src/core/include/deprecated/xrt.h b/runtime_src/core/include/deprecated/xrt.h
--- a/runtime_src/core/include/deprecated/xrt.h
+++ b/runtime_src/core/include/deprecated/xrt.h
@@ -623,7 +623,7 @@
  *
  */
-XCL_DRIVER_DLLHIDDEN
+XCL_DRIVER_DLLESPEC
 int
 xclIPName2Index(xclDeviceHandle handle, const char *ipName);
 
 /*
